age": {"code": "ug", "name": "Uyghur"}, "word": "رېئاللىق"}, {"language": {"code": "ug", "name": "Uyghur"}, "word": "ھەقىقەت"}, {"language": {"code": "uz", "name": "Uzbek"}, "word": "reallik"}, {"language": {"code": "uz", "name": "Uzbek"}, "word": "voqelik"}, {"language": {"code": "uz", "name": "Uzbek"}, "word": "haqiqat"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "thực tại"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "thực tế"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "hiện thực"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "The real world.", "tags": ["uncountable", "usually"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "A man very often fancies that he understands a critic, when in reality he does not comprehend his meaning.", "reference": "1712 February 12 (Gregorian calendar), [Joseph Addison; Richard Steele et al.], “FRIDAY, February 2, 1711–1712”, in The Spectator, number 291; republished in Alexander Chalmers, editor, The Spectator; a New Edition, […], volume III, New York, N.Y.: D[aniel] Appleton & Company, 1853, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "As a political system democracy seems to me extraordinarily foolish,[…]. My servant is, so far as I am concerned, welcome to as many votes as he can get.[…]I do not suppose that it matters much in reality whether laws are made by dukes or cornerboys, but I like, as far as possible, to associate with gentlemen in private life.", "reference": "1915, G[eorge] A. Birmingham [pseudonym; James Owen Hannay], chapter I, in Gossamer, New York, N.Y.: George H. Doran Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Does this mean that reality has caught up with science fiction?", "reference": "2015 August 13, Emmanuel Tsekleves, “Science fiction as fact: how desires drive discoveries”, in The Guardian, archived from the original on 18 Jun 2016:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A real entity, event, or other fact.", "tags": ["uncountable", "usually"], "examples": ["The ultimate reality of life is that it ends in death.", "There are several new realities that this team now needs to accept: our old project is dead, and our new project is now the priority."], "quotes": [{"text": "And to realities yield all her shows.", "reference": "1667, John Milton, “Book VII”, in Paradise Lost. […], London: […] [Samuel Simmons], and are to be sold by Peter Parker […]; [a]nd by Robert Boulter […]; [a]nd Matthias Walker, […], →OCLC; republished as Paradise Lost in Ten Books: […], London: Basil Montagu Pickering […], 1873, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "My neck, Sir, may be an idea to you, but to me it is a reality.", "reference": "1770, James Beattie, Essay on the Nature and Immutability of Truth:"}, {"text": "A dream, of simple fantasy / That I, wished was reality / That you'd, come knocking at my door / And we'd, relive this dream once more", "reference": "1983, Debarge, “A Dream”, in In A Special Way:"}, {"text": "Recent historical studies indicate that we must continue to challenge the notion that there is an unproblematic story of queer liberation. For example, how do local histories account for realities such as the increased racial segregation of the New York bar scene after Stonewall?", "reference": "1996 September, Doreen Drury, “The Gay Capital of the World”, in Gay Community News, page 22:"}, {"text": "Given the economic realities of contemporary Poland, a requirement to provide information on movable assets which exceed PLN 10,000 in value cannot be held to be excessive.", "reference": "2005 October 25, European Court of Human Rights, Wypych v. Poland, number 2428/05:"}, {"text": "Exploring alternative realities isn't just a game for boys. In 1666, Margaret Cavendish, the Duchess of Newcastle, published a utopian fantasy of compelling strangeness.", "reference": "2011 May 11, Sam Leith, “Sam Leith's top 10 alternative realities”, in The Guardian, archived from the original on 07 Mar 2021:"}, {"text": "It is time the international community faced the reality: we have an unmanageable, unfair, distortionary global tax regime. It is a tax system that is pivotal in creating the increasing inequality that marks most advanced countries today[…].", "reference": "2013 June 7, Joseph Stiglitz, “Globalisation is about taxes too”, in The Guardian Weekly, volume 188, number 26, archived from the original on 10 Apr 2021, page 19:"}, {"text": "But part of me was still glad to see this undoubtedly superficial take. As a society, we barely discuss the realities and implications of singledom. In pop culture singledom is almost invariably represented as an easily fixed unhappy state, a step along the way to getting happily hitched.", "reference": "2018 September 8, Sonia Sodha, “It’s time to ditch the stereotypes and look at the realities behind singledom”, in The Guardian, archived from the original on 09 Nov 2020:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "The entirety of all that is real.", "tags": ["uncountable", "usually"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Across the entire Universe. Never stopping, never faltering, never fading. People and planets and stars will become dust. And the dust will become atoms and the atoms will become... nothing. And the wavelength will continue, breaking through the rift at the heart of the Medusa Cascade into every dimension, every parallel, every single corner of creation. This is my ultimate victory, Doctor! The DESTRUCTION! Of REALITY! ITSELF!", "reference": "2008 July 5, Russell T Davies, “Journey's End”, in Graeme Harper, director, Doctor Who, season 4 [30], episode 13, spoken by Davros (Julian Bleach):"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "af", "name": "Afrikaans"}, "word": "realiteit"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "وَاقِع"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "իրական"}, {"language": {"code": "ba", "name": "Bashkir"}, "word": "ысынбарлыҡ"}, {"lang